(text "VIN, MODE and EN crossings have no junction: EN must remain separate from VIN.\nPlace both input capacitors at VIN/GND; use compact SW/inductor copper.\nKeep five output capacitors at the regulator. Route FB as a quiet Kelvin trace.\nMODE = VIN forces PWM. FSET = GND selects 2.25MHz and compensation1." (at 15.24 213.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a07ecc65-846a-5c9d-b228-aad0e5330f88"))
(text "10nF C0G: nominal 2.4ms soft start. 0.95V rail is cascaded from 3.3V for on-time margin.\n3.3V rail is dedicated to Ethernet and its core converter; do not export accessory power.\nPG does not guarantee Realtek voltage limits. Reset delay, controller connections and brownout re-arm remain unfinished.\nTI SLVSDU1K and Realtek RTL8125BG V1.5 / reference V122. See ethernet-power-qualification.json." (at 15.24 251.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "014d96d8-75a4-5200-8f6f-6d1c4419e9f6"))
